            "text": "Income that is just at or barely above the threshold carries significantly more risk than income with a clear margin above it. Consulate officers have some discretion, and an application where income is right at the minimum, after accounting for currency conversion and monthly variation, may be viewed as borderline. We recommend demonstrating income of at least 30-40% above the threshold minimum to create a genuine safety margin. If your income is close to the threshold, emphasise savings, additional assets, and consistency of income in your supporting evidence."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
